{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Only flesh with its life — its blood.</b> Its sense is thus: only flesh with its life, which is its blood, you shall not eat — like the sense of \"you shall not eat the life with the flesh\" (Deuteronomy 12:23), \"for the life of all flesh is its blood; it is as its life.\" And this life that moves and senses — it is the body."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:52.241867486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}